WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.781
It's been over 30 years since the original
Magnum, P.I. aired its final episode, but

00:00:04.781 --> 00:00:08.740
it's never too late to appreciate the lives
of the actors who helped bring this fun crime

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.860
series to life for millions of fans.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.060
From the leading man to the supporting characters,
here's what happened to the cast of Magnum,

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:15.580
P.I.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.680
Magnum, P.I. would've simply been impossible
without Thomas Sullivan Magnum IV, a Vietnam

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.880
war veteran-turned-private investigator.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.460
While sporting an exquisite mustache, Tom
Selleck pulled off this role with panache,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.700
while injecting his performance with a healthy
dose of rakish charm.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.480
Though Magnum remains Selleck's best-known
role, he'd already been acting for many years

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.000
prior on screens both big and small.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.740
And post-P.I., he's continued working consistently,
most recently as NYPD Police Commissioner

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.800
Frank Reagan in the CBS cop drama Blue Bloods.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.260
Outside of acting, he manages to keep himself
equally busy.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.860
In 2019, it was announced that he was working
on a memoir that would cover his fifty-year

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:59.579
showbiz career as well as his life outside
of the spotlight.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:05.020
“Magnum is still in a hundred countries,
and it's not dated.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.280
My shorts are dated.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.480
They're a little short."

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:13.420
One of Magnum's compatriots in his investigations
is helicopter charter pilot Theodore Calvin,

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.360
affectionately known as "T.C."

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.200
The beloved character was played by the now
mostly-retired Roger E. Mosley, who'd been

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.420
acting for nearly a decade before landing
the role.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.490
Though the bulk of his acting career ended
in 2010, he made a special appearance as barber

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.820
John Booky on the Magnum, P.I. reboot.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.360
This cameo surely provided longtime fans of
the original show a sense of amused satisfaction

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.780
as he bequeathed wisdom onto the new series'
T.C., played by Stephen Hill.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.880
Mosley's personal life is less in the news
these days than the more famous Selleck.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.399
But it's certainly worth noting that at the
time of shooting Magnum, P.I., he was actually

00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:55.090
a licensed helicopter pilot in real life,
Mosley turned 80 in 2018, and he's now living

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.909
in relative obscurity after a long and productive
career, hopefully enjoying his retirement

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:00.660
to the fullest.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:07.159
As played by Larry Manetti, Rick Wright was
the owner of the King Kamehameha Club, a favorite

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.240
hangout of Magnum's.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.720
Manetti had previously had recurring roles
on other TV series, including the original

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.740
Battlestar Galactica.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:18.580
But he's certainly best known for playing
Rick, a former war buddy of Magnum and T.C.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.330
Manetti continued acting up through 2016,
including a recurring role on the rebooted

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:28.080
Hawaii Five-O as Nicky Demarco, a star from
the eighties who excels at living the island

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.440
life, even when it's riddled with crime.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.580
In addition to acting, Manetti is the author
of the book Aloha Magnum, which details his

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.040
experiences on the set of Magnum, P.I.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.140
He's also the host of his own radio show on
CRN Talk Radio.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.500
And he even once had his hand in a real-life
restaurant, the Black Orchid in Honolulu,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:52.030
which he opened with Tom Selleck and Denver
Broncos owner Pat Bowlen in 1988 before eventually

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.600
selling the place in 1992.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:59.820
No relationship on Magnum, P.I. was as intriguing
to fans as the one between Magnum and John

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.980
Hillerman's Jonathan Quayle Higgins III.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:07.420
He was the caretaker of the beachfront estate
Robin's Nest, where Magnum led his leisurely

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:07.920
lifestyle.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.380
Magnum and Higgins start out the series at
odds, with Higgins's buttoned-up attitude

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.490
serving as a sharp contrast to Magnum's beer-swigging,
cap-wearing looseness.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:21.400
But in time, the two formed a begrudging respect
for each other, and that was in no small way

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.100
the result of Hillerman's fine acting abilities.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.720
Already a good deal older than his co-stars,
Hillerman brought British sophistication to

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.810
the show, despite actually hailing from Texas.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:36.120
He started his screen career in 1970, and
he had extensive theater experience before

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:36.620
that.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.420
He notched a fair share of notable supporting
roles in a number of classic films, such as

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.360
Chinatown and Blazing Saddles.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.200
Hillerman remained in Hollywood after Magnum,
P.I., though he never again took on any roles

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.510
that suited him quite as well as Higgins.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:56.450
He retired in 1999, with his last film credit
being 1996's A Very Brady Sequel.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.440
He passed away in 2017 at the age of 84.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.160
"My son was first mate on that boat.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.140
So thanks to you I'll never see my boy, Gilligan,
again."

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.020
What's a TV show about private investigators
without an attorney?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:15.410
Kathleen Lloyd played the recurring role of
assistant district attorney Carol Baldwin,

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:20.020
a good friend of Magnum's who tried to no
avail to pursue a romance with him.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.380
Interestingly enough, before taking on the
role of Carol, Lloyd made a guest appearance

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:28.440
in an earlier episode as a one-off character
named Bridget Archer.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:34.440
Lloyd had some notable credits before taking
on the part of Carol, including the 1976 Western

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.040
The Missouri Breaks alongside Marlon Brando
and Jack Nicholson.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.720
Younger audiences might recognize her post-P.I.
roles on such shows as The Practice and Babylon

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.220
5.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.840
Her last on-screen credit was in 2004, so
we hope she's been enjoying her retirement

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.100
from showbiz after nearly 35 years in the
industry!

